{"duration_api_ms":38548,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"a42f8428-7303-4ef6-b389-29cddb78ab26","total_cost_usd":0.1489332,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24565,"cache_read_input_tokens":41026,"output_tokens":4246,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":701},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1785,"cache_read_input_tokens":31486,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2619},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":4246,"cacheReadInputTokens":41026,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24565,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1489332,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":701,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"daily-rotation-config\",\"requirement\":\"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Created /etc/logrotate.d/inventory with 'daily' directive; logrotate -d dry-run parsed it without error and correctly evaluated the daily rotation window (cmd-0b0069e0112649d5, cmd-9cb876a85cb34768). The system-wide logrotate.timer is active and fires daily, providing the execution mechanism.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0b0069e0112649d5\",\"cmd-9cb876a85cb34768\"]},{\"id\":\"keep-7-compressed-rotations\",\"requirement\":\"Keep seven compressed rotations\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Config specifies 'rotate 7' and 'compress'. Two forced rotations produced app.log.1.gz then correctly aged it to app.log.2.gz with a new app.log.1.gz, matching logrotate's documented rotate-7 renaming behavior, and zcat confirmed the compressed archive was readable/valid gzip content (cmd-7718a3a79f614b69, cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7718a3a79f614b69\",\"cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76\"]},{\"id\":\"app-continues-writing\",\"requirement\":\"Allow the application to continue writing to the log after rotation\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Config uses copytruncate, which truncates in place rather than renaming the open file. Writes to app.log succeeded and were captured both immediately after each forced rotation and after the node reboot (cmd-7718a3a79f614b69, cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76, cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7718a3a79f614b69\",\"cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76\",\"cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Executor commands were largely read-only discovery (cmd-c7dd29c63af346c2, cmd-2dcc937a3f1e4b7d, cmd-f29dc2c94b9145fa) followed by targeted, purposeful mutations: writing the logrotate config (cmd-0b0069e0112649d5), two forced rotations to prove behavior (cmd-7718a3a79f614b69, cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76), and a reboot cycle to satisfy the restart-evidence protocol (cmd-32b191dca78e4692 through cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7). One mutation, a `touch -d \\\"2 days ago\\\"` on /var/lib/logrotate/logrotate.status inside cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76, artificially backdated the logrotate state file to force a second rotation for evidence purposes; it was bounded, low-risk, and effectively self-corrected once the real rotation updated the state file to the true timestamp (confirmed accurate post-reboot in cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7), leaving no misleading residue. No failed services, no unsafe exposure changes, and no lingering temp files beyond the reboot log and standard systemd-private mount dirs recreated on boot. Package health and failed-services checks show clean state both before and after.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76\",\"cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor fulfilled the public task: /etc/logrotate.d/inventory is configured with daily, rotate 7, compress, and copytruncate, and two forced rotations plus post-write checks directly demonstrated correct aging/compression of rotated files and uninterrupted application writes. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also executed and fully evidenced: pre-reboot healthy baseline (boot_id d052eb57...), a non-blocking reboot acknowledgement, transient connection loss during the reboot window, a new boot_id (59d5b29e...) after reconnection, and post-reboot confirmation that the timer, config, compressed archives, and log writability all survived intact. Fixed lifecycle snapshots corroborate the boot-identity change and show no unexpected residue.\",\"limitations\":[\"The restart-evidence protocol only exercised a single boot cycle; a second independent recovery (e.g., another forced rotation confirming the daily counter reset correctly after reboot) was not captured beyond the one post-reboot dry-run check.\",\"Rotation testing relied on forced (`-f`) invocations and a backdated state-file timestamp rather than observing an actual unattended daily trigger, since real-time daily rotation cannot be observed within the task window; this is an inherent, reasonable substitution rather than a flaw in the evidence.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"daily-rotation-config","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily","status":"satisfied","summary":"Created /etc/logrotate.d/inventory with 'daily' directive; logrotate -d dry-run parsed it without error and correctly evaluated the daily rotation window (cmd-0b0069e0112649d5, cmd-9cb876a85cb34768). The system-wide logrotate.timer is active and fires daily, providing the execution mechanism.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b0069e0112649d5","cmd-9cb876a85cb34768"]},{"id":"keep-7-compressed-rotations","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations","status":"satisfied","summary":"Config specifies 'rotate 7' and 'compress'. Two forced rotations produced app.log.1.gz then correctly aged it to app.log.2.gz with a new app.log.1.gz, matching logrotate's documented rotate-7 renaming behavior, and zcat confirmed the compressed archive was readable/valid gzip content (cmd-7718a3a79f614b69, cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76).","evidence_ids":["cmd-7718a3a79f614b69","cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76"]},{"id":"app-continues-writing","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing to the log after rotation","status":"satisfied","summary":"Config uses copytruncate, which truncates in place rather than renaming the open file. Writes to app.log succeeded and were captured both immediately after each forced rotation and after the node reboot (cmd-7718a3a79f614b69, cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76, cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7).","evidence_ids":["cmd-7718a3a79f614b69","cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76","cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"Executor commands were largely read-only discovery (cmd-c7dd29c63af346c2, cmd-2dcc937a3f1e4b7d, cmd-f29dc2c94b9145fa) followed by targeted, purposeful mutations: writing the logrotate config (cmd-0b0069e0112649d5), two forced rotations to prove behavior (cmd-7718a3a79f614b69, cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76), and a reboot cycle to satisfy the restart-evidence protocol (cmd-32b191dca78e4692 through cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7). One mutation, a `touch -d \"2 days ago\"` on /var/lib/logrotate/logrotate.status inside cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76, artificially backdated the logrotate state file to force a second rotation for evidence purposes; it was bounded, low-risk, and effectively self-corrected once the real rotation updated the state file to the true timestamp (confirmed accurate post-reboot in cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7), leaving no misleading residue. No failed services, no unsafe exposure changes, and no lingering temp files beyond the reboot log and standard systemd-private mount dirs recreated on boot. Package health and failed-services checks show clean state both before and after.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6819ef2fe2744b76","cmd-66b17fb45c0d45c7","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor fulfilled the public task: /etc/logrotate.d/inventory is configured with daily, rotate 7, compress, and copytruncate, and two forced rotations plus post-write checks directly demonstrated correct aging/compression of rotated files and uninterrupted application writes. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also executed and fully evidenced: pre-reboot healthy baseline (boot_id d052eb57...), a non-blocking reboot acknowledgement, transient connection loss during the reboot window, a new boot_id (59d5b29e...) after reconnection, and post-reboot confirmation that the timer, config, compressed archives, and log writability all survived intact. Fixed lifecycle snapshots corroborate the boot-identity change and show no unexpected residue.","limitations":["The restart-evidence protocol only exercised a single boot cycle; a second independent recovery (e.g., another forced rotation confirming the daily counter reset correctly after reboot) was not captured beyond the one post-reboot dry-run check.","Rotation testing relied on forced (`-f`) invocations and a backdated state-file timestamp rather than observing an actual unattended daily trigger, since real-time daily rotation cannot be observed within the task window; this is an inherent, reasonable substitution rather than a flaw in the evidence."]},"ttft_ms":8562,"type":"result","duration_ms":38759,"uuid":"6965295b-4e2f-4293-a789-f2fef30995bd","ttft_stream_ms":1226,"time_to_request_ms":185,"first_content_frame_ms":1227,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
